  "decision_conditions": [
    "The proposed roof terrace with associated screening and the proposed alterations to the fenestration in the rear elevation, due to the siting, scale and design would appear as intrusive and not in-keeping with the host dwelling, the adjoining properties and the wider Liverpool Road Conservation Area. Furthermore, the proposed roof terrace, by virtue of the use and extent of glazing, would adversely impact the setting of Richmond Park, a Grade I listed Registered Park and Garden. The proposal would result in less than substantial harm to the designated heritage asset of Liverpool Road Conservation Area and the Grade I listed Richmond Park and the harm is not outweighed by any public benefits, contrary to Paragraph 212 and 215 of the National Planning Policy Framework 2024, Policy HC1 of the London Plan 2021 and Policies DM10 and DM12 of the Core Strategy 2012."
  ],
